{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/tests/goldens.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.876830Z","id":"90dc27fe91be1e899722d2c632c25e2ad63fd31e69ff09b5a00af5dc4cd8d8ee","body":{"detail":"If a second #[test] is added to this file, the env writes race its threads. Keep one test per binary, or move the stores into an argument the pipeline threads through.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"dc4bcb594f6f16fdb896fb1931054d14025b7294123b4247ecb340edf0ca1c27"},"summary":"The test sets HOME and every agent store with std::env::set_var (unsafe in edition 2024) before the glob; sound only while this binary has one test","tags":["goldens","test-hygiene","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/tests/goldens.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.756028Z","id":"53729a2d268d88790984d31c1c9017be54c263551aa3989a2a7efd40eaf4cd36","body":{"detail":"If a second #[test] is added to this file, the env writes race its threads. Keep one test per binary, or move the stores into an argument the pipeline threads through (the opencode store already is: pipeline::opencode_store roots it in scratch).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"dc4bcb594f6f16fdb896fb1931054d14025b7294123b4247ecb340edf0ca1c27"},"summary":"The test sets HOME and every agent store with std::env::set_var (unsafe in edition 2024) before the globs; sound only while this binary has one test","supersedes":"90dc27fe91be1e899722d2c632c25e2ad63fd31e69ff09b5a00af5dc4cd8d8ee","tags":["goldens","test-hygiene","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/tests/regressions.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:48:36.341578Z","id":"8ec243bc084316d15cdabca05935ff299392d9407c999671fd2e5efce7634f12","body":{"detail":"Each set is one transcript file; session chains and rotation artifacts are never read by the pipeline, so dropping a whole segment cannot fail here. Covered only by crates/toolpath-claude/src/chain.rs test_orphaned_stem_is_not_a_successor. To close: a chained set (goldens/claude-chain/: predecessor + successor + .orphaned-* stem) read through read_conversation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"2ebe9a6d6abb316b782bf9945125221b250cc637d2b1fd9ddb7069efa0eebc5f"},"summary":"The goldens do not reach Claude .orphaned-* rotation (#236, toolpath-claude 0.13.1)","tags":["regression-corpus","gap","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/tests/regressions.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:48:36.362824Z","id":"c226e4b928a439c169dda92f74dd2c38a769157b1a95cd2a2d1a3999f133f558","body":{"detail":"It is path-cli export/resume behaviour against an existing session file, not a pipeline stage. Covered by crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs export_claude_refuses_existing_session_without_force. To close: a golden that exports a set over its own source in a temp project and requires the refusal (and the resume-picks-local rule).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"2ebe9a6d6abb316b782bf9945125221b250cc637d2b1fd9ddb7069efa0eebc5f"},"summary":"The goldens do not reach the export clobber of a richer local original (2026-07-30)","tags":["regression-corpus","gap","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/tests/regressions.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:48:36.382585Z","id":"d66327a3cb41fead5f47cc470bcee4f0d705a452ec43c6ae855b7aba09ace04b","body":{"detail":"The cursor set is a JSON dump of a CursorSession, not a database, so a reader regression on the 3.24 table cannot fail here. Covered by crates/toolpath-cursor/src/reader.rs reads_heads_from_the_3_24_table. To close: a database-shaped cursor set (as opencode_db.rs does for opencode).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"2ebe9a6d6abb316b782bf9945125221b250cc637d2b1fd9ddb7069efa0eebc5f"},"summary":"The goldens do not reach Cursor's state.vscdb (3.24 composerHeaders)","tags":["regression-corpus","gap","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/tests/goldens.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:01:06.846503Z","id":"2414bd5b143e09fc2a229f820da7bdd55324ff23099f0e3c018c5394c6420657","body":{"detail":"If a second #[test] is added to this file, the env writes race its threads. Keep one test per binary, or move the stores into an argument the pipeline threads through (the opencode store already is: pipeline::opencode_store roots it in scratch).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":173},"end":{"line":173},"content_hash":"dc4bcb594f6f16fdb896fb1931054d14025b7294123b4247ecb340edf0ca1c27"},"summary":"The test sets HOME and every agent store with std::env::set_var (unsafe in edition 2024) before the globs; sound only while this binary has one test","supersedes":"53729a2d268d88790984d31c1c9017be54c263551aa3989a2a7efd40eaf4cd36","tags":["goldens","test-hygiene","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/tests/schemas.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:26:03.116248Z","id":"baa7a7b57845cd6b98a0bffae8b2644a7cef2a5ad35e53ae6a13d4a196099eb1","body":{"detail":"The ir@<recording> snapshot body is a toolpath-convo ConversationView. toolpath-convo derives no JsonSchema and the kind spec describes the document, not the view, so every_snapshot_matches_its_kind skips ir@. A schemars derive on ConversationView (and Turn, Usage, the event and tool types) would close it; it touches the shared crate every harness uses, so it is its own piece.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"723633ea717167f8d0561071a2bf59dc8afb561bb4f69b8a190be3d254a542e4"},"summary":"ir@ snapshots have no JSON Schema: ConversationView has none","tags":["baseline","schema","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/tests/goldens.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:53:04.541651Z","id":"94f2a9e173a3187b208be640fe44bc59765a7d529c084c4cc20404eb3f102c8f","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The binary now has one test per recording. HOME and every agent store are set once inside a OnceLock (homes()) that every test enters before reading the environment, so the env writes happen before any other test reads it (pr/50).","supersedes":"2414bd5b143e09fc2a229f820da7bdd55324ff23099f0e3c018c5394c6420657","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
